", "url": "https://news.google.?oc=5"}, {"title": "Ohio poll: Democrats lead, but voters expect Republicans to win Senate, governor’s races", "source": "NBC4 WCMH-TV", "published": "2026-09-17T07:00:00+00:00", "url": "https://news.google.?oc=5"}], "model": {"prior_margin": 0.79, "prior_sd": 5.0, "poll_margin": 4.53, "poll_sd": 4.97, "poll_weight": 0.5, "fundamentals": {"margin": -0.28, "lean": -5.0, "environment": 7.38, "incumbency": -3.0, "money": 0.34}, "rating_margin": 1.5, "sigma_race": 5.5, "sigma_total": 6.28, "baseline_margin": 2.67, "analyst_adjustment": -0.17, "key_factors": ["Polling average shows Brown ahead by roughly 3-5 points, though the most recent Quantus poll has the race tied", "Prediction markets price Brown at about 57-60%, consistent with a modest Democratic edge", "Husted holds incumbency and strong cash-on-hand, but Brown has outraised him heavily and faces heavy outside spending", "Ohio's Republican-leaning fundamentals (PVI R+5) cap Brown's advantage"], "rationale": "Recent polls mostly show Brown up three to five points, with the newest poll tied, and markets price him near 58%. Weighing that against Ohio's Republican lean, Husted's incumbency and the heavy outside spending against Brown, a narrow Democratic edge of about two to three points fits the evidence.", "watch": "A late shift on the economy and cost-of-living messaging, or further pro-Husted outside spending, could tighten this into a true tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Jon Husted (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Ohio's special Senate race pits appointed Republican incumbent Jon Husted against former Senator Sherrod Brown in a contest most raters call a tossup, though a few lean Democratic. Polling through late September shows Brown ahead by a few points in most surveys, with the newest poll showing a dead heat. Brown has raised far more money than Husted, but Trump-linked PACs and crypto-industry groups have spent heavily against him.\n\nThe race sits in a